---

<ArticleLayout
    title={title}
    description={description}
    author={author}
    authorUrl={authorUrl}
    pubDate={pubDate}
    readingTime={readingTime}
    image={image}
    imageAlt={imageAlt}
    category="Security"
    categorySlug="tools/vpn"
    headings={headings}
>
  <!-- Introduction -->
  <h2 id="introduction">The Truth About VPN Speeds</h2>
  <p>
    Every VPN provider claims to be the "fastest." Marketing departments love throwing around phrases like
    "lightning-fast speeds" and "no lag." But what do the numbers actually say?
  </p>
  <p>
    We ran over 500 speed tests across 10 popular VPNs to cut through the marketing and find out which
    services actually deliver the best performance for remote workers. Our testing covered servers in
    North America, Europe, and Asia during peak and off-peak hours.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>The bottom line:</strong> The best VPNs only reduce your speed by 10-15%. The worst can cut
    your bandwidth in half. Here's exactly what we found.
  </p>

  <!-- Speed Test Results -->
  <h2 id="speed-results">Speed Test Results</h2>
  <p>
    Baseline speed (no VPN): <strong>500 Mbps download / 50 Mbps upload</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    All tests conducted using the WireGuard protocol where available, connecting to the nearest
    recommended server.
  </p>

  <ComparisonTable columns={speedColumns} rows={speedRows}/>

  <p>
    <strong>Key takeaway:</strong> NordVPN and ExpressVPN consistently delivered the fastest speeds,
    with less than 15% speed loss. Budget options like Surfshark also performed well, making them
    excellent value for the price.
  </p>

  <!-- Testing Methodology -->
  <h2 id="methodology">How We Tested</h2>
  <p>
    Speed tests are only meaningful with consistent methodology. Here's how we ensured fair comparisons:
  </p>

  <h3>Test Environment</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Connection:</strong> 500 Mbps fiber connection (US East Coast)</li>
    <li><strong>Hardware:</strong> MacBook Pro M2, Windows 11 desktop</li>
    <li><strong>Testing tool:</strong> Speedtest.net and fast.com (averaged)</li>
    <li><strong>Protocol:</strong> WireGuard/NordLynx where available, OpenVPN otherwise</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Test Parameters</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>5 tests per server location, averaged</li>
    <li>Tests run at 9 AM, 2 PM, and 8 PM local time</li>
    <li>Server locations: US (New York, LA), UK (London), Germany (Frankfurt), Singapore</li>
    <li>All VPNs tested on same day to control for network conditions</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>What We Measured</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Download speed:</strong> Most important for streaming and browsing</li>
    <li><strong>Upload speed:</strong> Critical for video calls and file sharing</li>
    <li><strong>Ping/latency:</strong> Affects real-time applications like video calls</li>
    <li><strong>Consistency:</strong> How much speeds varied between tests</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- Fastest VPNs Ranked -->
  <h2 id="rankings">Fastest VPNs Ranked</h2>

  <h3>1. NordVPN - Best Overall Speed</h3>
  <p>
    NordVPN's proprietary NordLynx protocol (based on WireGuard) consistently delivered the fastest
    speeds in our testing. With only 11% speed loss on average, you'll barely notice the VPN is running.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Avg speed loss:</strong> 11%</li>
    <li><strong>Best for:</strong> HD video calls, streaming, large file transfers</li>
    <li><strong>Standout:</strong> NordLynx protocol outperformed all competitors</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <a href="/go/nordvpn" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="text-jet-stream hover:text-sky-light">
      Get NordVPN (68% off) &rarr;
    </a>
  </p>

  <h3>2. ExpressVPN - Most Consistent</h3>
  <p>
    ExpressVPN's Lightway protocol delivered excellent speeds with the most consistent performance
    across all server locations. Great choice if you frequently switch between regions.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Avg speed loss:</strong> 14%</li>
    <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Users who need reliability across many countries</li>
    <li><strong>Standout:</strong> Most consistent speeds regardless of server location</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <a href="/go/expressvpn" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="text-jet-stream hover:text-sky-light">
      Try ExpressVPN risk-free &rarr;
    </a>
  </p>

  <h3>3. Surfshark - Best Budget Speed</h3>
  <p>
    Surfshark proves you don't need to pay premium prices for fast VPN speeds. At under $2.50/month,
    it outperformed several more expensive options.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Avg speed loss:</strong> 18%</li>
    <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Budget-conscious users who still want good performance</li>
    <li><strong>Standout:</strong> Unlimited device connections included</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <a href="/go/surfshark" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="text-jet-stream hover:text-sky-light">
      Get Surfshark (81% off) &rarr;
    </a>
  </p>

  <!-- What Affects VPN Speed -->
  <h2 id="speed-factors">What Affects VPN Speed</h2>
  <p>
    Understanding these factors helps you get the best performance from any VPN:
  </p>

  <h3>Server Distance</h3>
  <p>
    Data has to travel to the VPN server before reaching its destination. A server 500 miles away
    will be faster than one 5,000 miles away. Always connect to the nearest server unless you need
    a specific location.
  </p>

  <h3>Server Load</h3>
  <p>
    Popular servers get crowded. If a server shows 80%+ capacity, try another one in the same region.
    Most VPN apps display server load—use it.
  </p>

  <h3>VPN Protocol</h3>
  <p>
    Modern protocols make a huge difference:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>WireGuard/NordLynx:</strong> Fastest, recommended for most users</li>
    <li><strong>IKEv2:</strong> Fast, good for mobile devices</li>
    <li><strong>OpenVPN:</strong> Slower but most compatible</li>
    <li><strong>PPTP:</strong> Fast but insecure—avoid</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Encryption Level</h3>
  <p>
    Stronger encryption requires more processing. AES-256 (the standard) offers excellent security
    with minimal speed impact on modern devices.
  </p>

  <h3>Your Base Internet Speed</h3>
  <p>
    A 15% speed loss on a 500 Mbps connection is different than on a 50 Mbps connection. If your
    base speed is slow, VPN overhead becomes more noticeable.
  </p>

  <!-- Tips for Faster Speeds -->
  <h2 id="speed-tips">Tips for Faster VPN Speeds</h2>

  <h3>1. Use WireGuard Protocol</h3>
  <p>
    If your VPN offers WireGuard (called NordLynx on NordVPN, Lightway on ExpressVPN), use it.
    It's significantly faster than OpenVPN with equivalent security.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Connect to Nearby Servers</h3>
  <p>
    Use your VPN's "Quick Connect" or "Smart Location" feature. These automatically select the
    fastest server for your location.
  </p>

  <h3>3. Try Different Servers</h3>
  <p>
    If one server is slow, try another in the same city or region. Server performance varies
    based on load and routing.
  </p>

  <h3>4. Check for ISP Throttling</h3>
  <p>
    Run a speed test with and without VPN. If VPN speeds are actually better for certain activities
    (streaming, torrenting), your ISP may be throttling that traffic.
  </p>

  <h3>5. Use Wired Connection</h3>
  <p>
    WiFi adds latency and variability. For the most stable VPN speeds, use an ethernet cable when possible.
  </p>

  <h3>6. Close Background Apps</h3>
  <p>
    Other apps using bandwidth (cloud sync, updates, streaming) compete with your VPN connection.
    Close unnecessary apps for maximum speed.
  </p>

  <!-- FAQ Section -->
  <FAQSection faqs={faqs}/>

  <!-- Conclusion -->
  <h2 id="conclusion">Our Speed Verdict</h2>
  <p>
    For remote workers who need fast, reliable VPN speeds:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Best overall:</strong> <a href="/go/nordvpn" rel="nofollow sponsored">NordVPN</a> - fastest speeds with
      NordLynx protocol
    </li>
    <li><strong>Most consistent:</strong> <a href="/go/expressvpn" rel="nofollow sponsored">ExpressVPN</a> - reliable
      performance worldwide
    </li>
    <li><strong>Best value:</strong> <a href="/go/surfshark" rel="nofollow sponsored">Surfshark</a> - great speeds at
      budget prices
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The speed differences between top VPNs are small enough that other factors—like security features,
    server locations, and price—should also influence your decision. Check our
    <a href="/tools/best-vpn-digital-nomads">complete VPN comparison guide</a> for full reviews.
  </p>
  <p>
    All three top performers offer money-back guarantees, so you can test speeds on your own
    connection risk-free.
  </p>

  <!-- Related Articles -->
  <Fragment slot="full-width">
    <RelatedArticles articles={relatedArticles}/>
  </Fragment>
</ArticleLayout>
